artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider classical 10-dimensional string backgrounds describing a compactification of the form M_4 × M_6, where M_4 is 4-dimensional de Sitter spacetime and M_6 is a compact internal 6-manifold, sourced by D-branes and orientifold planes, together with NSNS and RR p-form fluxes obeying the type II supergravity equations of motion (with localized brane/orientifold sources) and admitting a (positive) 4d cosmological constant.

Such a solution is said to be controlled as a genuine classical string background if it simultaneously satisfies the following four properties:
(i) Large internal volume: the volume Vol(M_6), measured in string units, is parametrically large (so that α′ and higher-derivative corrections are negligible);
(ii) Small string coupling: the (spatial average of the) dilaton e^{φ} is parametrically small (so that string-loop corrections are negligible);
(iii) Bounded number of orientifolds: the total orientifold charge (equivalently, the number of orientifold planes required by the tadpole condition) is bounded by a fixed integer independent of any tunable parameter;
(iv) Quantized fluxes: all p-form flux quanta lie in the integer Dirac-quantization lattice (and remain finite integers as parameters are tuned).

Question: Does there exist a classical de Sitter solution of this type that simultaneously satisfies (i)–(iv), or is this combination of four properties impossible?

